------------------------------------ |\n9: | hooks               | Yes, project plugin in `.amp/plugins/entire.ts`                   |\n10: | transcript_analyzer | Yes, parses `.entire/tmp/amp/*.jsonl` captured from plugin events |\n11: | compact_transcript  | Yes, emits Entire compact transcript JSONL for checkpoints v2     |\n12: | token_calculator    | No, Amp plugin events do not expose token usage                   |\n13: \n14: ## Installation\n15: \n16: ```bash\n17: cd agents/entire-agent-amp\n18: go build -o entire-agent-amp ./cmd/entire-agent-amp\n19: cp entire-agent-amp /usr/local/bin/\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Or use mise:\n23: \n24: ```bash\n25: cd agents/entire-agent-amp\n26: mise run build\n27: ```\n28: \n29: ## Prerequisites\n30: \n31: - Amp CLI installed as `amp` on `PATH`.\n32: - Amp must be launched with `PLUGINS=all` for project plugins to load except for users using the [Neo](https://ampcode.com/news/neo) version of Amp, which supports project plugins without the env var.\n33: \n34: ## How It Works\n35: \n36: `install-hooks` creates `.amp/plugins/entire.ts`. The plugin forwards Amp lifecycle events to `entire hooks amp \u003cevent\u003e`:\n37: \n38: | Amp Event                                                         | Protocol Event        |\n39: | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n40: | synthetic `session.start` before first `agent.start` for a thread | SessionStart (type 1) |\n41: | `agent.start`                                                     | TurnStart (type 2)    |\n42: | `agent.end`                                                       | TurnEnd (type 3)      |\n43: \n44: Amp does store native transcript files locally, threads are serverside. The plugin payloads are therefore cached as JSONL under `.entire/tmp/amp/\u003cthread-id\u003e.jsonl`, and that cache is used for transcript analysis and compact checkpoint transcripts.\n45: \n46: ## Development\n47: \n48: ```bash\n49: go build -o entire-agent-amp ./cmd/entire-agent-amp\n50: go test ./...\n51: external-agents-tests verify ./entire-agent-amp\n52: \n53: cd ../../\n54: E2E_AGENT=amp mise run test:e2e\n55: ```"},"status":"done"},{"type":"tool_result","toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_014esrwMNRSRuDcV4Ai57AAa","output":{"absolutePath":"/Users/savekirk/dev/ai/entire/external-agents/agents/entire-agent-amp/AGENT.md","content":"1: # Amp — External Agent Research\n2: \n3: ## Verdict: COMPATIBLE\n4: \n5: Amp has a TypeScript plugin system with lifecycle events for `agent.start` and `agent.end`. Project plugins require launching Amp with `PLUGINS=all`. The public plugin API does not expose a stable native transcript file path, so the integration captures event/message payloads into `.entire/tmp/amp/*.jsonl` and implements transcript analysis from that cache.\n6: \n7: ## Static Checks\n8: | Check | Result | Notes |\n9: |-------|--------|-------|\n10: | Binary present | PASS | `amp` found locally |\n11: | Help available | PASS | `amp --help` |\n12: | Version info | PASS | `amp --version` |\n13: | Hook keywords | PASS | Plugin docs provide lifecycle events |\n14: | Session keywords | PASS | `threads continue`, `threads export` |\n15: | Config directory | PASS | `~/.config/amp` documented |\n16: | Documentation | PASS | https://ampcode.com/manual/plugins.md and https://ampcode.com/manual/plugin-api.md |\n17: \n18: ## Binary\n19: - Name: `amp`\n20: - Install: Amp CLI from AmpCode distribution.\n21: - Plugin loading: run `PLUGINS=all amp ...`.\n22: \n23: ## Hook Mechanism\n24: - Config file: `.amp/plugins/entire.ts`\n25: - Config format: TypeScript plugin running on Amp's Bun-provided runtime.\n26: - Hook registration: plugin default export receives `PluginAPI`, registers handlers with `amp.on(event, handler)`.\n27: - Hook names and protocol mapping:\n28: \n29: | Native Hook Name | When It Fires | Protocol Event Type |\n30: |------------------|---------------|---------------------|\n31: | synthetic `session.start` | before first `agent.start` per thread | 1 = SessionStart |\n32: | `agent.start` | user submits a prompt | 2 = TurnStart |\n33: | `agent.end` | agent finishes a turn | 3 = TurnEnd |\n34: \n35: `session.start` from Amp itself does not always include `thread.id`, so the plugin does not rely on it for session identity.\n36: \n37: ## Session Management\n38: - Session ID source: Amp `thread.id`.\n39: - Session directory: `.entire/tmp/amp/`.\n40: - Session file format: JSONL cache written by the external agent binary from hook payloads.\n41: - Resume mechanism: `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue \u003cthread-id\u003e`.\n42: \n43: ## Transcript\n44: - Location: `.entire/tmp/amp/\u003csafe-thread-id\u003e.jsonl`.\n45: - Format: JSONL with `agent.start` and `agent.end` entries.\n46: - User prompt field: `agent.start.message`.\n47: - Modified files field: `agent.end.modified_files`, populated via `amp.helpers.filesModifiedByToolCall`.\n48: - Token usage field: unavailable in documented plugin events.\n49: \n50: ## Protocol Mapping\n51: | Subcommand | Native Concept | Implementation Notes | Feasibility |\n52: |-----------|----------------|----------------------|-------------|\n53: | `info` | static metadata | Return name `amp`, capabilities | Required |\n54: | `detect` | `amp` binary | Check `command -v amp` | Required |\n55: | `get-session-id` | Amp thread ID | Read from hook input | Required |\n56: | `get-session-dir` | `.entire/tmp` | Standard Entire temp dir | Required |\n57: | `resolve-session-file` | `.entire/tmp/\u003cid\u003e.json` | Standard path resolution | Required |\n58: | `read-session` | cached JSONL | Build AgentSession from cache | Required |\n59: | `write-session` | cached JSONL | Write native data to session ref | Required |\n60: | `read-transcript` | cached JSONL | Return raw bytes | Required |\n61: | `chunk-transcript` | raw bytes | Base64 chunking via protocol JSON encoding | Required |\n62: | `reassemble-transcript` | chunks | Reassemble raw bytes | Required |\n63: | `format-resume-command` | Amp thread continue | `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue \u003cid\u003e` | Required |\n64: | `parse-hook` | plugin event JSON | Map hook payloads to protocol events | Hooks |\n65: | `install-hooks` | project plugin | Write `.amp/plugins/entire.ts` | Hooks |\n66: | `uninstall-hooks` | project plugin | Remove `.amp/plugins/entire.ts` | Hooks |\n67: | `are-hooks-installed` | project plugin | Check plugin marker | Hooks |\n68: | `get-transcript-position` | JSONL line count | Return line count offset | Transcript analyzer |\n69: | `extract-modified-files` | plugin helper output | Read `modified_files` arrays | Transcript analyzer |\n70: | `extract-prompts` | `agent.start` entries | Read prompt text | Transcript analyzer |\n71: | `extract-summary` | last assistant text | Read last assistant text block from `agent.end.messages` | Transcript analyzer |\n72: | `compact-transcript` | cached messages | Emit Entire compact JSONL | Compact transcript |\n73: \n74: ## Selected Capabilities\n75: | Capability | Declared | Justification |\n76: |-----------|----------|---------------|\n77: | hooks | true | Amp plugins expose lifecycle events |\n78: | transcript_analyzer | true | Plugin captures enough prompt/message/file data |\n79: | compact_transcript | true | Captured messages map to Entire compact transcript format |\n80: | transcript_preparer | false | Cache is directly readable |\n81: | token_calculator | false | Token usage is not documented in plugin events |\n82: | text_generator | false | Amp CLI is used for agent execution, not summary generation |\n83: | hook_response_writer | false | Not needed for lifecycle hooks |\n84: | subagent_aware_extractor | false | No documented subagent transcript tree |\n85: \n86: ## Gaps \u0026 Limitations\n87: - Amp must be launched with `PLUGINS=all` for hooks to fire.\n88: - Transcript data is plugin-captured, not a documented native Amp session file.\n89: - Token usage is not available from documented plugin event payloads.\n90: - `session.start` cannot be trusted for thread identity because `thread.id` is optional there.\n91: \n92: ## E2E Test Prerequisites\n93: - Entire CLI binary: `entire` from PATH or `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`.\n94: - Agent CLI binary: `amp`.\n95: - Non-interactive prompt command: `PLUGINS=all amp --dangerously-allow-all --no-notifications --no-ide -x '\u003cprompt\u003e'`.\n96: - Interactive mode: `PLUGINS=all amp`.\n97: - Expected prompt pattern: `\u003e`.\n98: - Timeout multiplier: 1.5.","discoveredGuidanceFiles":[{"uri":"file:///Users/savekirk/dev/ai/entire/external-agents/agents/entire-agent-amp/AGENT.md","lineCount":99,"content":"# Amp — External Agent Research\n\n## Verdict: COMPATIBLE\n\nAmp has a TypeScript plugin system with lifecycle events for `agent.start` and `agent.end`. Project plugins require launching Amp with `PLUGINS=all`. The public plugin API does not expose a stable native transcript file path, so the integration captures event/message payloads into `.entire/tmp/amp/*.jsonl` and implements transcript analysis from that cache.\n\n## Static Checks\n| Check | Result | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| Binary present | PASS | `amp` found locally |\n| Help available | PASS | `amp --help` |\n| Version info | PASS | `amp --version` |\n| Hook keywords | PASS | Plugin docs provide lifecycle events |\n| Session keywords | PASS | `threads continue`, `threads export` |\n| Config directory | PASS | `~/.config/amp` documented |\n| Documentation | PASS | https://ampcode.com/manual/plugins.md and https://ampcode.com/manual/plugin-api.md |\n\n## Binary\n- Name: `amp`\n- Install: Amp CLI from AmpCode distribution.\n- Plugin loading: run `PLUGINS=all amp ...`.\n\n## Hook Mechanism\n- Config file: `.amp/plugins/entire.ts`\n- Config format: TypeScript plugin running on Amp's Bun-provided runtime.\n- Hook registration: plugin default export receives `PluginAPI`, registers handlers with `amp.on(event, handler)`.\n- Hook names and protocol mapping:\n\n| Native Hook Name | When It Fires | Protocol Event Type |\n|------------------|---------------|---------------------|\n| synthetic `session.start` | before first `agent.start` per thread | 1 = SessionStart |\n| `agent.start` | user submits a prompt | 2 = TurnStart |\n| `agent.end` | agent finishes a turn | 3 = TurnEnd |\n\n`session.start` from Amp itself does not always include `thread.id`, so the plugin does not rely on it for session identity.\n\n## Session Management\n- Session ID source: Amp `thread.id`.\n- Session directory: `.entire/tmp/amp/`.\n- Session file format: JSONL cache written by the external agent binary from hook payloads.\n- Resume mechanism: `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue \u003cthread-id\u003e`.\n\n## Transcript\n- Location: `.entire/tmp/amp/\u003csafe-thread-id\u003e.jsonl`.\n- Format: JSONL with `agent.start` and `agent.end` entries.\n- User prompt field: `agent.start.message`.\n- Modified files field: `agent.end.modified_files`, populated via `amp.helpers.filesModifiedByToolCall`.\n- Token usage field: unavailable in documented plugin events.\n\n## Protocol Mapping\n| Subcommand | Native Concept | Implementation Notes | Feasibility |\n|-----------|----------------|----------------------|-------------|\n| `info` | static metadata | Return name `amp`, capabilities | Required |\n| `detect` | `amp` binary | Check `command -v amp` | Required |\n| `get-session-id` | Amp thread ID | Read from hook input | Required |\n| `get-session-dir` | `.entire/tmp` | Standard Entire temp dir | Required |\n| `resolve-session-file` | `.entire/tmp/\u003cid\u003e.json` | Standard path resolution | Required |\n| `read-session` | cached JSONL | Build AgentSession from cache | Required |\n| `write-session` | cached JSONL | Write native data to session ref | Required |\n| `read-transcript` | cached JSONL | Return raw bytes | Required |\n| `chunk-transcript` | raw bytes | Base64 chunking via protocol JSON encoding | Required |\n| `reassemble-transcript` | chunks |